<title>ISRAEL: Delek Fuel 1996 EPS 10.96 shekels.</title>
<headline>Delek Fuel 1996 EPS 10.96 shekels.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-03-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delek The Israel Fuel Corp.</p>
<p>			   (in thousands of shekels except EPS)</p>
<p>			   Q4 96	Q4 95    12-MTH 96    12-MTH 95</p>
<p>Revenue		655,941	n/a	2,268,004    2,467,840</p>
<p>Operating profit    53,859	n/a	  198,595	100,427</p>
<p>Net Profit	    23,182	n/a	  105,608	102,240</p>
<p>Earnings per share    2.41	n/a	    10.96	  10.61</p>
<p>Revenue figures are net of customs and purchase taxes.</p>
<p>Delek, Israel's third-largest fuel distributor, said the 98 percent rise in its operating profit was due to a &quot;significant&quot; improvement in profitability at its Delek Motors unit, which is the Israeli agent for Mazda.</p>
<p>However, attributable earnings from affiliated companies fell by 60.5 percent to 23.566 million shekels in 1996, mainly from declining profits at Israel Petrochemical Industries. Losses from minorities tripled to 20.67 million shekels.</p>
<p>Delek said its board would recommend a final dividend of an aggregate 15.031 million shekels. Together with an interim dividend declared earlier, the total payout for the year will be 23.824 million shekels.</p>
<p>($1=3.37 shekels)</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
